<ServiceLayout title="Vertigo" description="Chiropractic treatment for vertigo and dizziness at Frey Clinic of Chiropractic in Napoleon, OH." schemaType="MedicalCondition">
<p>Vertigo — the sensation that you or your surroundings are spinning — can be disorienting and debilitating. While vertigo has several possible causes, many cases are related to the upper cervical spine and respond well to chiropractic care.</p>
<hr class="rule rule--accent" style="margin-block:var(--sp-6);" />
<h2>The cervical connection</h2>
<p>The upper cervical spine plays a critical role in balance and spatial orientation. Misalignment in this area can affect the nerves and blood vessels that serve the inner ear and vestibular system. By correcting these misalignments, chiropractic care can help reduce or eliminate vertigo episodes.</p>
<h2>Our approach</h2>
<p>We begin with a careful evaluation to understand the nature and cause of your vertigo. If cervical misalignment is involved, gentle upper cervical adjustments can often provide significant relief. We may also recommend specific exercises to support vestibular function.</p>
</ServiceLayout>
